TOUCH(1)                     Funny CLI Manual                     TOUCH(1)

NAME
    touch — Create a file, or update its timestamp, because sometimes
    you just need something to exist.

SYNOPSIS
    touch <file>

DESCRIPTION
    The touch command creates an empty file at the specified path if it
    does not already exist.

    If the provided name does not contain a file extension, .txt is
    automatically added.

    If the file already exists, touch leaves its contents unchanged.

USAGE
    > touch <file>       # Creates the specified file.
    > touch notes        # Creates notes.txt.
    > touch notes.txt    # Creates notes.txt.

FUN FACTS
    - touch does not actually touch anything.
    - Files without an extension automatically become .txt files.
    - Creating an existing file does not erase its contents.
    - Sometimes creating an empty file is the first step toward
    creating something much less empty.

EXAMPLES
    > touch notes
        Creates an empty file called notes.txt.

    > touch notes.txt
        Creates an empty file called notes.txt.

    > touch /home/user/config.txt
        Creates config.txt inside /home/user.

    > touch notes.txt
        Leaves the existing file and its contents unchanged.

SEE ALSO
    help(1), ls(1), cat(1), rm(1), mkdir(1), man(1)

    Remember, touch creates the file.
    What you put inside it is your problem.

